.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-84-
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-85-- No unresolved product or architecture choice remains in this story. The accepted research fixes schema 6, `go-v1`, build roots, all byte algorithms, protected-state provenance, dry-run, manager-home isolation, marker v2, receipt v1, and the claim transition.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md:86:- Executable upstream gates remain explicit at task granularity: shared-vector consumption is blocked by `TASK-260720-3ag6pi` — Verify integrated protocol v6 conformance, and downstream documentation waits for `TASK-260720-3lo9jc` — Document schema v6 authoring and CLI behavior. Coarse story links to the protocol and Curator implementations are intentionally omitted at handoff: the former duplicates these exact gates, while the latter would couple an explicitly independent Python implementation to reference-manager code. `STORY-260720-21bsr2` remains blocked by both manager stories and owns cross-manager sequencing. No duplicate clarification task is needed.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md:87:- The local cocoaskills clone is clean but behind `origin/main` by two commits. Every implementation task checklist requires fast-forwarding the clean clone before its task worktree and then basing on all dependency handoffs.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-88-- Windows DACL and reparse-safe access are implementation-heavy but not a human decision boundary. The platform task has a fail-closed backend contract and dedicated Windows CI acceptance criteria.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-89-- The protocol rc.4 suite is not landed yet. The conformance and CI tasks explicitly forbid pinning an unreleased or fabricated commit and wait for the immutable upstream verification task.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md:90:- The current cocoaskills CI has pytest, strict mypy, build, and twine gates but no separately configured lint command. Final verification runs any lint gate that exists by execution time and records the current absence instead of inventing release evidence.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-91-- Existing implementation anomalies are tracked in the owning tasks: consumer state is written before materialization, runtime reuse trusts an existing directory without required-path validation, materialization is not transaction-wide, and project/global dry-run currently enters a file-creating global lock while the registry path can persist cache/state.
.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_decomposition-plan.md-92-- Existing unrelated board validation anomalies remain out of scope. Planning validation reports them separately and does not alter unrelated board items.
--
